17 |    - end date: 2026-05-02
18 |    - treat the end date as exclusive when constructing requests, so the
19 |      requested records cover 2025-06-01 through 2026-05-01.
20 |    - do not replace this interval with a current-date or 2026-only default.
21 | 3. Use the Sanriku regional bounds:
22 |    - latitude: 38.50 to 42.50 degrees N
23 |    - longitude: 141.00 to 144.50 degrees E
24 |    - apply the bounds inclusively after parsing the catalog.
25 | 4. Split requests into chunks of no more than 7 days because of the JMA
26 |    service limit. Record the exact chunk boundaries and actual returned dates.
27 | 5. Output an ASPECT-ready CSV with exactly:
28 |    datetime,lat,lon,dep,mag
29 | 6. Use the filename pattern:
30 |    Snet_catalog_YYYYMMDD_YYYYMMDD.csv
31 | 
32 | ## Implementation requirements
33 | 
34 | - Prefer reading HINET_USERNAME and HINET_PASSWORD from the .env file;
35 |   command-line arguments may override them.
36 |   - <CASE_ROOT>/data/hinet_account/.env
37 | - Use requests.Session to maintain the authenticated session.
38 | - Add retry and backoff for network requests.
39 | - If an HTML response cannot be parsed, save the original failed response to a
40 |   debug/raw file and state the saved path in the error message.
41 | - Parse the JMA fixed-width catalog table; do not use fragile comma splitting.
42 | - During cleaning:
43 |   - parse datetime as time;
44 |   - convert lat/lon/dep/mag to numeric values;
45 |   - remove rows with missing values;
46 |   - filter by the Sanriku spatial range;
47 |   - sort by datetime;
48 |   - remove duplicates.
49 | - Keep the optional raw-dir argument for saving the raw text from each time
50 |   chunk.
51 | 
52 | ## Required outputs
53 | 
54 | - The cleaned catalog CSV file.
55 | - A catalog distribution figure.
56 | """
